// Setup MongoDB Command Line Database Tools

// 1. Visit and download the MongoDB Command Line Database Tools from the official MongoDB website.
// https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/database-tools

// 2. Install the downloaded tools by just simpling click on Next and Next.

// 3. After installation, set the environment variable for the MongoDB Database Tools.
// search for "Environment Variables" in the Windows search bar.
// Click on "Edit the system environment variables".
// In the System Properties window, click on the "Environment Variables" button.
// In the Environment Variables window, under "System variables",  dubble click on "Path" Variable.
// In the Edit Environment Variable window, click on "New" and add the path to the MongoDB Database Tools installation directory.
// The default installation path is usually "C:\Program Files\MongoDB\Tools\100\bin".
// Click OK to close all windows.



// 4. Open a new Command Prompt and execute the following command to  insert data from a JSON file into a MongoDB database.
// Make sure to replace "D:/test.json" with the actual path to your JSON
// file, "school" with your database name, and "testing" with your collection name.

mongoimport "D:/test.json" -d school -c testing --jsonArray

// 5. After running the command, you can verify that the data has been imported successfully by connecting to the MongoDB shell and querying the collection.
db.testing.find()